{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/678530-question-about-true-fae","id":678530,"title":"Question about True Fae","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-25T22:10:36-07:00","id":678530,"title":"Question about True Fae","content":"So, I don't think I quite have a handle on how powerful the true fae can be outside of Arcadia. Are they as powerful as they want to be, as powerful as the plot demands, or are there actual limitations on what they can do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T22:38:55-07:00","id":678558,"title":"","content":"They are specifically not as powerful as they want to be outside of Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Fae outside of Faerie are essentially Changeling's equivalent of Royal Avatars \u2014 they're still significant threats for any but the most experienced group of changelings, but they lack access to the godlike powers of their core being. Autumn Nightmares covers the behavior of the Fae on Earth and in the Hedge and dreams, though 2e's decreased emphasis on the Fae as direct antagonists may render this information less useful in the long run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T22:44:01-07:00","id":678559,"title":"","content":"In 1E, their power outside of Arcadia is determined by the number of Titles they possess, Actors(and Props and Wisps) in the range of Wyrd 6-10 respectively always. Their attribute/ contracts, and other scales are accorded to this. For more, read Equinox Road(With advisement from Autumn Nightmares).<br /> <br /> In 2E,....Well, Dave hasn't talked 2E Strangers yet, so I can't talk about their default mode, though my advisement for them is, mostly, run. However, in a maintained freehold, they are actively limited by the Approaches set by the Freehold, the Courts, and the Courtiers with a high enough Mantle. They <i>must</i> fulfill each one as is relevant. Most don't bother and send Huntsmen and Loyalists who can ignore Approaches. So, either ZOM, A G! or possibly really tripped up....or dangerously savvy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T03:59:26-07:00","id":688105,"title":"","content":"Outside Arcadia they can be relatively weak. Even in the Edge.<br /> <br /> Check the demo:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/28293/Changeling-The-Lost-Demo?it=1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/1/28293.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/28293/Changeling-The-Lost-Demo?it=1\" target=\"_blank\"> Changeling: The Lost Demo - White Wolf | Changeling: The Lost | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/28293/Changeling-The-Lost-Demo?it=1\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/28293/Changeling-The-Lost-Demo?it=1 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Changeling: The Lost Demo - This free booklet gives you and five of your friends everything you need to play your first game of Changeling:The Lost, </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7277-brighella","name":"Brighella","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T08:25:42-07:00","id":688364,"title":"","content":"THe demo is not a reliable product anymore. :/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T15:48:53-07:00","id":688937,"title":"","content":"Not everyone have all manuals, and if he ask that question probably he has just the core.<br /> And not all the Fae are immensively strong, narrators can choose. Can they, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7277-brighella","name":"Brighella","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T19:14:53-07:00","id":689089,"title":"","content":"There's more in this than might be thought. Let me break into it.<br /> <br /> 1)True, not everyone has all the supplements, and the standard, right now, is the first edition core book, which does not stipulate a Wyrd level, though examples are fairly high in there.<br /> <br /> 2)Strictly speaking still, the game's assumption within canon is that a Stranger's incarnations <i>are</i> immensely powerful. But as you say, there's not a clear line of explanation in just the core alone.<br /> <br /> 3)As always, a GM has the right to just do what they want.<br /> <br /> 4)Changeling has various levels of authority when it comes to Stranger creation, with the core, Autumn Nightmares, and Equinox Road all positing different things and the latter two written with the assumption of surplanting the core books' rules.. Equinox Road is the most defined and comprehensive, and so if we ignore the core book base assumption, it's the clearest authority, and that books says the minimum a True Fae can even be is Wyrd 5, and they have to be in a shitty, shitty place for that to be the case. The way this book is written is to strongly suggest it to be the default canon as soon as one owns it, which is creates a kerfuffle for the entire &quot;Only the core book is considered needed&quot; attitude.<br /> <br /> 5)Certainly within fandom discussion that uses canon as a centerpole for discussion and the basis for deviation, Equinox Road is treated as the authority above the core. Any conversation within the fandom quickly shifts attention over to that book.<br /> <br /> 6)Changeling Second Edition has a very....<i>definite</i> stance about this, with an emphasis on making them the big bad in the background, more menacing as an atmospheric element than an active piece on the board. I can't explain what exactly this stance is in mechanical terms, so I will simply say this- unless you are pretty damn powerful yourself or have a really damn good plan or argument for your freedom(and a way to get that argument out), your default answer when dealing with them should always fall on the side of running the hell away. You can fight a Hobgoblin, a Fetch, a Loyalist, or even a Huntsman, but only legends and lucky kids get away with confronting the True Fae when they move.<br /> <br /> TL; DR, First Edition is a kerfuffle that heavily relies on the idea that True Fae are powerful but doesn't necessarily enforce it, Second Edition does not have weak Strangers. All of this can be ignored if you're willing to ignore canon, which is certainly the right of any play group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T23:04:05-07:00","id":689351,"title":"","content":"Must the Stranger give at least an opportunity (albeit very small) to the changeling contester to archieve victory , if only because the Wyrd hates invincible villains ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T00:25:23-07:00","id":689392,"title":"","content":"It always struck me that a True Fae should never really be met as an antagonist, they seem for the most part completely uncaring one of their toys has left, which adds to the horror of a changeling completely traumatised and living an existence of fear and doing/avoiding things to keep from being recaptured... But their Keeper doesn't actually give a shit and has already forgotten about them.<br /> <br /> Thats not the case all the time, there are Privateers out there which are a far more common antagonist, after all... Though there's something just dark about the above which just works in a Changeling chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T08:36:41-07:00","id":689758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/678530-question-about-true-fae?p=689351#post689351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Must the Stranger give at least an opportunity (albeit very small) to the changeling contester to archieve victory , if only because the Wyrd hates invincible villains ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. The True Fae has weaknesses baked in, given what they are, but a True Fae never has to pull their punch. From their perspective, the game's already set, and a person's inability to play it is no excuse for losing the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T10:12:03-07:00","id":689856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/678530-question-about-true-fae?p=678559#post678559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Most don't bother and send Huntsmen and Loyalists who can ignore Approaches. So, either ZOM, A G! or possibly really tripped up....or dangerously savvy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huntsman ignore approaches? Who exactly is bound by them then if the True Fae send agents and the agents ignore them?<br /> <br /> Or did you mean that Huntsmen only need to fufill X Approaches where True Fae need to fufill all of them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T11:27:41-07:00","id":689928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/678530-question-about-true-fae?p=689856#post689856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huntsman ignore approaches? Who exactly is bound by them then if the True Fae send agents and the agents ignore them?<br /> <br /> Or did you mean that Huntsmen only need to fufill X Approaches where True Fae need to fufill all of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>From the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-court-creation-and-toronto/\" target=\"_blank\">Courts teaser</a>, a Huntsman gets a point of Yearning if abiding by an Approach. The impression the piece left is that a Huntsman isn't barred from coming at the Changeling from another angle, they just won't get a point of Yearning from it. That said, the text does stress that Huntsmen usually do abide by Approaches, so we can presume Yearning is a big deal for them. Just not a 100% guarantee to the Lost. Particularly if the True Fey is offering a Huntsman a sufficiently juicy reward for that Changeling.<br /> <br /> Hmm... I remember also seeing some mention of defense or bonus against opposition from (I think) the True Fey (or at least attempts to take Changelings back) if a Bulwark was active, but I'm failing to find it now. Can't really say how that played out, if it <i>was</i> True Fey only, or interacted in some way with the fulfillment of Approaches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T12:25:18-07:00","id":690098,"title":"","content":"What Gaius said. A Huntsman is going to want to keep to the script some of the time so they can get Yearnings(which are very important), but they don't <i>have to</i>. A Huntsman who thinks they can just get the job done without them can completely ignore them and go for it....but said Huntsman might find themselves not equal to the task. Yearnings are potent, yo. So while a Huntsman is encouraged to go down certain troughs, they can hop out when the time is right, but by that point you should know they're coming.<br /> <br /> As for the True Fae, as mentioned, something that didn't come across in the first draft is that the True Fae <i>have to</i> obey all Approaches that pertain to what they're doing. Also, courtiers receive a defense bonus equal to their mantle against True Fae","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T18:12:16-07:00","id":690669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/678530-question-about-true-fae?p=690098#post690098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Gaius said. A Huntsman is going to want to keep to the script some of the time so they can get Yearnings(which are very important), but they don't <i>have to</i>. A Huntsman who thinks they can just get the job done without them can completely ignore them and go for it....but said Huntsman might find themselves not equal to the task. Yearnings are potent, yo. So while a Huntsman is encouraged to go down certain troughs, they can hop out when the time is right, but by that point you should know they're coming.<br /> <br /> As for the True Fae, as mentioned, something that didn't come across in the first draft is that the True Fae <i>have to</i> obey all Approaches that pertain to what they're doing. Also, courtiers receive a defense bonus equal to their mantle against True Fae</div> </div> </div> </div>So a Huntsman can cheat, but they get punished for it by being, well, two-bit hobgoblin hired guns without ammo.<br /> <br /> I like it. Keeps players on their toes while also keeping Huntsmen with an obvious, universal weakness changelings can out-think (and explains why the True Fae keep hiring them no matter how many times their asses are kicked).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T02:51:45-07:00","id":690994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/678530-question-about-true-fae?p=689392#post689392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It always struck me that a True Fae should never really be met as an antagonist, they seem for the most part completely uncaring one of their toys has left, which adds to the horror of a changeling completely traumatised and living an existence of fear and doing/avoiding things to keep from being recaptured... But their Keeper doesn't actually give a shit and has already forgotten about them.<br /> <br /> Thats not the case all the time, there are Privateers out there which are a far more common antagonist, after all... Though there's something just dark about the above which just works in a Changeling chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is not about the prize, but the game itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T04:13:35-07:00","id":691020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/678530-question-about-true-fae?p=689758#post689758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. The True Fae has weaknesses baked in, given what they are, but a True Fae never has to pull their punch. From their perspective, the game's already set, and a person's inability to play it is no excuse for losing the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... a possible interesting departure from the necessary stance of the Gentry in relation to the preferences of the Wyrd far as 1st edition material is concerned.<br /> <br /> Do I understand it correctly that the difference is, while they still require narrative reenaction and meaningful* conflict, the latter does not need to be fair? As opposed to the necessity to satisfy the minimum standards of a 'fair' engagement lest their efforts be pointless and their identities, as they were, eventually dissolve back into the Wyrd from lack of definition.<br /> <br /> *For a given definition of meaningful. Equinox Road and Autumn Nightmares seemed to emphasize it as requiring an actual possibility of defeat, no matter how small, but it's absolutely possible to conceive of meaningful conflict that is neither fair nor uncertain in resolution. If it is truthful and has significance to someone, I would consider it meaningful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 10-06-2015, 07:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T10:00:37-07:00","id":691373,"title":"","content":"The rules in regards to the True Fae are fairly light in 2E(Like, serious mechanics for them are summed up in a paragraph), and in their lightness there's real brutality. It really is intended to keep them in the background and terrifying when they take center stage. There's a reason we have Huntsmen(who are also brutal in the sharpest, most conniving ways possible-but they are manageable).<br /> <br /> Stuff like Equinox Road's logic can apply, there's no reason for it not to, but the game's about fairy tales, and never has any fairy played fair unless it was fun to do so(usually in service to their hubris).<br /> <br /> Consider, for a second, the simple act of stealing a person and turning them into a changeling to begin with. A mortal can take advantage of their Frailities as much as anyone else-certainly years of them going at it has left the tools lying around <i>somewhere</i>. Even if it doesn't, mortals can learn from observation what those are. They still can process information from a Domain to figure a way out. The answers are <i>there</i>.<br /> <br /> But would you ever call the act of kidnapping people <i>fair</i>? Would you ever call a Durance <i>fair? </i><br /> <br /> Course not. The True Fae do what changelings do-they stack the deck in their favor as best they can, and they have a great many cards to play. Changelings might have the ability to hide cards in their sleeves where the True Fae don't, but the True Fae know every card so well that they probably don't need to. That's not to say that loopholes don't exist-changelings <i>break free</i> after all. That's not to say you can't break the game-changelings <i>kill True Fae </i>time from time. But if you think you're outside the game and it turns out you're not, gods help you.<br /> <br /> It's like tossing someone into a game of DnD and expecting someone to win against the dragon without <i>telling</i> them what to do. Everything you need is there, theoretically. Pay close attention and work it out, you might do it it. You learn the game by watching how others play it, you explore your options, maybe you get the skill checks, figure out that, hey, there's a hole in the monster's breast, and finally stab the hell out of it with a spear. But it'd be easier if someone let you at least read the books first, but nope, the DM's an asshole. You can figure out the rules as you play.<br /> <br /> That's the True Fae. They have their games, they have their rules, they have their weaknesses. They play in accordance to them, always, at pain of oblivion, but they never, <i>ever</i> play them fair.<br /> <br /> EDIT: So next time a True Fae comes in and has to play in accordance to <i>every damn Approach you have</i>, take some time to laugh at them. Where they can't hear you, of course.<br /> <br /> And then you should murderkill them with iron before they get the chance to make your life miserable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-06-2015, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T11:40:38-07:00","id":691473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/678530-question-about-true-fae?p=691020#post691020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do I understand it correctly that the difference is, while they still require narrative reenaction and meaningful* conflict, the latter does not need to be fair? As opposed to the necessity to satisfy the minimum standards of a 'fair' engagement lest their efforts be pointless and their identities, as they were, eventually dissolve back into the Wyrd from lack of definition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm on the tail end of Equinox Road in my readthrough, so I think it's all right for me to chime in here as regards 1e Fae:<br /> <br /> All the stuff about struggle is in the section talking about Legends and the limits of manifestation \u2014 Realms can't be literally inescapable or merciless deathtraps or even unacceptably inconvenient, Props can't have unknowable weaknesses or primary powers that cover every facet of their use, Actors and Wisps have finite stats and dicepools within a scope typically slightly above that of a powerful PC's range \u2014 it's a note that the Fae can never be omnilaterally superlative and that their traps and defenses are fallible; the <i>Wild Hunt</i> is an explicit means of feeding the need for narrative conflict, and a Fae in Realm form literally holds the power of life and death over their slaves.<br /> <br /> The force that drives the Fae forbids them from turning every conflict into a juggernaut roll or a clash of unstoppable-force-meets-immovable-object. It means the tools to thwart them at any given time <i>exist</i>, not that they're all within immediate reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T12:53:51-07:00","id":691613,"title":"","content":"What Satchel says applies to something I've been thinking about since last post.<br /> <br /> The mechanics are brutal, but the mentality of the fae is the same as Equinox Road, summed up as Satchel puts it-the means are always there, just not always immediately in reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T13:56:39-07:00","id":691688,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers, Arc! (And thanks for chiming in Satchel.) That is honestly a bit enlightening, and it remindeds me of some very pertinent details about the True Fae. There are things I sometimes overlook, and in this case I got slightly tunnel visioned on the writing (though the last time I read the core being years ago didn't help). My bias for Equinox Road definitely played a part; it's one of my top WoD books ever, so I rely on it over most of the other CtL books in terms of the Others.<br /> <br /> You've made things clearer for me now. Had kinda lost part of the context there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T20:49:13-07:00","id":691947,"title":"","content":"Although I like Equinox Roads a lot, I felt like the book fell down a bit when it came to the mechanics for Actor manifestations. They're basically just powerful Changelings with a few minor differences (e.g. Immortal Flesh, Ruled by Passion, ability to change Kiths, flexible Contracts). Not nearly as cool as the rules (particularly Mien Blessings) from Autumn Nightmares, in my opinion. And The example Other in the book, The Baroness of Tortured Harmonies, possesses 3 special traits (similar to what Grim Fears calls Fae Aspects), but, when discussing creating Actors, ER doesn't even mention that they might possess other traits like that, much less provide a list of them to use or advice on creating your own. <br /> <br /> I always looked at the various versions of the Gentry from 1e as a set of options to choose from, rather than revisions intended to usurp the earlier iterations. Especially since Equinox Roads references Autumn Nightmares and the core and tells you to use whichever version works best for the story you're telling (see &quot;Variations on the Theme&quot; after The Baroness's description in Chapter 4). Then there's the fact that Grim Fears, which came out just after ER, seems to ignore both Autumn Nightmares and Equinox Roads and presents True Fae in nearly the same format as the core book (with the exception of calling their innate powers Fae Aspects). In my games, I like to use most of the rules from ER, but create Actors more along the lines of Autumn Nightmares with a touch of Grim Fears here and there.<br /> <br /> Even if you're taking Equinox Road as the definitive authority on the True Fae, it still leaves open the vague possibility of weaker True Fae, since an Actor can grow weaker if it is on Earth for awhile (like the Exiled). There's no mechanics presented, but I think it's fair to guess that this could reduce their Wyrd below 5. These are still True Fae, but they could be considerably weaker. I also feel like an Actor formed from a Title that's Dwindling could be considerably weaker, but that's just a pet theory. It could provide for an interesting story where Changelings actively attempt to frustrate a Fae's attempts to forge Legends somehow, so that they can weaken an Actor enough to destroy it. There's also the possibility of players facing an Actor that's popped up as an independent being after being lost to Dwindling by one of the Others. Such a creature probably thinks it's a &quot;real&quot; True Fae, and I don't see why the players wouldn't as well.<br /> <br /> I don't see any reason to retcon away Blue Jenny's Keeper from the venerable demo. She could be a True Fae that's already significantly weakened in some way (Exiled, Dwindled, hobbled by some sort of pledge that weakens her significantly in the mortal world, already injured for some reason, etc.). Besides, even if she's defeated, she's only &quot;killed&quot;, not killed. Side note: Weirdly, my copies of the quickstart don't actually list her Wyrd score at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T20:51:41-07:00","id":691957,"title":"","content":"So, let's see if I understood what is in store for True Fae in 2ED. They are meant to be used sparingly, influence the plot through pawns and be like what Tv Tropes defines as <b><a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=PzqkQPD-bMY\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;The Dreaded&quot;</a>.</b> Good examples of how 2ED Gentry are supposed to affect the game's events and atmosphere include Hermaeus Mora, Nyarlathotep and the Slender Man. Their Huntsmen would be Miraak, cultists in general and the Proxies, respectively. Alternatively, Nyarlathotep is a very powerful Huntsman, and the True Fae it is serving is Yog-Sothoth/Azathoth. Another source of inspiration would be the G-Man, who serves ominous and nebulous forces while choosing to abide by &quot;certain restrictions&quot;, as he puts it. Sounds like a Huntsman to me.<br /> <br /> All of these examples are analogies, though. For instance, Nyarlathotep works better as a Qashmal, God-Machine Angel (or the Unchained version thereof), or even a Mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 10-07-2015, 03:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T07:53:11-07:00","id":692472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/678530-question-about-true-fae?p=691947#post691947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see any reason to retcon away Blue Jenny's Keeper from the venerable demo. She could be a True Fae that's already significantly weakened in some way (Exiled, Dwindled, hobbled by some sort of pledge that weakens her significantly in the mortal world, already injured for some reason, etc.). Besides, even if she's defeated, she's only &quot;killed&quot;, not killed. Side note: Weirdly, my copies of the quickstart don't actually list her Wyrd score at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no reason you can't do that. It's just not the default assumption of any book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T08:24:17-07:00","id":692503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/678530-question-about-true-fae?p=692472#post692472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no reason you can't do that. It's just not the default assumption of any book.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to me like the default assumption of Equinox Roads is that the Actor template provided is a rough guideline rather than a hard and fast power benchmark and that there are reasons (particularly prolonged time on Earth) that any given manifestation might be weaker. It seems weird that the default assumption would be to invalidate old material rather than just assuming the old material represents a variation, exception, or special circumstance. Especially given the aforementioned &quot;Variations on the Theme&quot; segment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T19:59:33-07:00","id":870867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/678530-question-about-true-fae?p=689089#post689089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's more in this than might be thought. Let me break into it.<br /> <br /> 1)True, not everyone has all the supplements, and the standard, right now, is the first edition core book, which does not stipulate a Wyrd level, though examples are fairly high in there.<br /> <br /> 2)Strictly speaking still, the game's assumption within canon is that a Stranger's incarnations <i>are</i> immensely powerful. But as you say, there's not a clear line of explanation in just the core alone.<br /> <br /> 3)As always, a GM has the right to just do what they want.<br /> <br /> 4)Changeling has various levels of authority when it comes to Stranger creation, with the core, Autumn Nightmares, and Equinox Road all positing different things and the latter two written with the assumption of surplanting the core books' rules.. Equinox Road is the most defined and comprehensive, and so if we ignore the core book base assumption, it's the clearest authority, and that books says the minimum a True Fae can even be is Wyrd 5, and they have to be in a shitty, shitty place for that to be the case. The way this book is written is to strongly suggest it to be the default canon as soon as one owns it, which is creates a kerfuffle for the entire &quot;Only the core book is considered needed&quot; attitude.<br /> <br /> 5)Certainly within fandom discussion that uses canon as a centerpole for discussion and the basis for deviation, Equinox Road is treated as the authority above the core. Any conversation within the fandom quickly shifts attention over to that book.<br /> <br /> 6)Changeling Second Edition has a very....<i>opdefinite</i> stance about this, with an emphasis on making them the big bad in the background, more menacing as an atmospheric element than an active piece on the board. I can't explain what exactly this stance is in mechanical terms, so I will simply say this- unless you are pretty damn powerful yourself or have a really damn good plan or argument for your freedom(and a way to get that argument out), your default answer when dealing with them should always fall on the side of running the hell away. You can fight a Hobgoblin, a Fetch, a Loyalist, or even a Huntsman, but only legends and lucky kids get away with confronting the True Fae when they move.<br /> <br /> TL; DR, First Edition is a kerfuffle that heavily relies on the idea that True Fae are powerful but doesn't necessarily enforce it, Second Edition does not have weak Strangers. All of this can be ignored if you're willing to ignore canon, which is certainly the right of any play group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there any open development posts about the true faerie and their mechanics by now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T20:18:08-07:00","id":870873,"title":"","content":"Not yet. Will there be?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://s2.quickmeme.com/img/51/51a1622a91d17e6e18a434f07c59d7fcb7b274c857c2db4de72f2e68c1de74ac.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T20:36:32-07:00","id":870887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/678530-question-about-true-fae?p=870873#post870873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not yet. Will there be?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://s2.quickmeme.com/img/51/51a1622a91d17e6e18a434f07c59d7fcb7b274c857c2db4de72f2e68c1de74ac.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Now there's a meme that I missed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T08:57:58-07:00","id":871318,"title":"","content":"I think asking for mechanics for the True Fae is missing the point. You don't defeat the True Fae by throwing enough dice at them, you defeat them narratively. You trap them in a story where the only narrative choice for them is to <i>accept</i> defeat. It doesn't matter how you do it, whether you set them up to be the villain that your motley of heroes defeat, or they sets themselves up to be a hero and you weave a masterful subversion where the villains (your motley) win.<br /> <br /> Defeating a True Fae means staring at them in the eyes and saying, &quot;I think we both know how this story goes.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T12:30:11-07:00","id":871601,"title":"","content":"Thing of the matter is that Dave said that if I wanted to, I could go ahead and toss it up. I actually have the power to do that.<br /> <br /> But I'm not going to for a few reasons.<br /> <br /> 1) It's the True Fae, man, that should totally be toted out by the Dev himself, you know what I'm saying? Wouldn't be cool if I did it.<br /> <br /> 2) I have to think long and hard about what's going on with open playtests and what we're trying to test. The average game, as this point, shouldn't <i>have</i> a True Fae present-it's enough that you know that they linger in the background like a towering doom. What players should be testing against is the Huntsmen and other changelings, seeing how the character mechanics work for players and storyteller. By keeping them out of the picture, we incentivize more changelings, more experimentation and playing around with the player mechanics, and in particular get feedback from storyteller on how it works from the other side of the wall. By keeping them out of the picture, we're more likely to get feedback on the Huntsmen in play, if for no other reason than people will grudgingly use them. Introduce the True Fae, and we lose a really good opportunity to get more information. It's not much of a thing, but it's important for keeping the playtests on track with the goals of the playtests.<br /> <br /> 3) Even if I did put them up, I'm not sure how much use the players would get out of it. The True Fae are....<br /> <br /> Well, I'm not going to tell you low-powered changelings can't beat them. They can. Is it hard? Oh yeah, but the way the True Fae are setup, that curve exists even if you're a high powered changeling, and high powered games are actually not a norm for most gamers. It's possible to have a fun game with the True Fae present, and even win.<br /> <br /> But I honestly think that if you guys could look at the True Fae's mechanics, you'd leave them in the background. I think there is a real chance that the response is &quot;Oh shit, do not touch.&quot; On a milder approach to it, I'm just not sure what the average group of players would do with them. Not in the sense of I can't imagine uses, but in that I have trouble seeing groups going ahead with those uses. It gives me enough pause that I don't feel bad about not being the one to pull the trigger on that.<br /> <br /> The wheels are turning behind the scenes, and while I don't know when the playtests'll be done, it doesn't strike me as implausible that very soon some of my opinions about the timing of the True Fae's reveal will change. Because, yeah, we do want you people to playtest these guys too. There's a time for them, though.<br /> <br /> I think that hour is sooner than I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T19:30:10-07:00","id":872816,"title":"","content":"Without True Fae mechanics, I don't know how much use Faerie Favor \u2022\u2022\u2022 merit is going to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T18:00:56-07:00","id":879136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/678530-question-about-true-fae?p=872816#post872816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without True Fae mechanics, I don't know how much use Faerie Favor \u2022\u2022\u2022 merit is going to be.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm pretty sure it can mimic the Miracle Dread Power in most ways. I don't think it's a stretch to say you can ask for things like &quot;a 5 dot Token that does this and that&quot; or even &quot;help me and my motley kill this other True Fae&quot;. Instead of destroying one of your Aspirations, the drawback of Faerie Favor is that other changelings might suspect you're a Loyalist and act accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T03:26:13-07:00","id":881628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/678530-question-about-true-fae?p=879136#post879136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm pretty sure it can mimic the Miracle Dread Power in most ways. I don't think it's a stretch to say you can ask for things like &amp;quot;a 5 dot Token that does this and that&amp;quot; or even &amp;quot;help me and my motley kill this other True Fae&amp;quot;. Instead of destroying one of your Aspirations, the drawback of Faerie Favor is that other changelings might suspect you're a Loyalist and act accordingly.</div> </div> </div> </div> Only if you get caught.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T07:59:24-07:00","id":881790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/678530-question-about-true-fae?p=881628#post881628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only if you get caught.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you have to roll some sort of mental + social combo to see if anyone suspects you each time you use it? With a bigger penalty each time? I mean, you can only get so much free stuff out of nowhere or be mysteriously saved so many times before people start getting suspicious. And Changelings are very paranoid about Loyalists to begin with anyway.<br /> <br /> Also, Faerie Favor sounds like a Loyalist merit. Maybe they could even get it for a reduced price","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T10:29:42-07:00","id":881956,"title":"","content":"Actually a cool thing would be to do a very powerful and short term goblin vow for the three dot Faire Favour, then call in the favour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T10:33:56-07:00","id":881959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/678530-question-about-true-fae?p=881790#post881790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe you have to roll some sort of mental + social combo to see if anyone suspects you each time you use it? With a bigger penalty each time? I mean, you can only get so much free stuff out of nowhere or be mysteriously saved so many times before people start getting suspicious. And Changelings are very paranoid about Loyalists to begin with anyway.<br /> <br /> Also, Faerie Favor sounds like a Loyalist merit. Maybe they could even get it for a reduced price</div> </div> </div> </div> It depends on how careful you are and how public the favour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T20:45:23-07:00","id":882503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/678530-question-about-true-fae?p=881959#post881959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends on how careful you are and how public the favour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but a paranoid Freehold is going to be suspicious of anyone who cheats death too many times or shows up with one too many powerful tokens, no matter how good his excuse is this time<br /> <br /> There's always the chance they never suspect you at all though, which is why you roll","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T12:57:32-07:00","id":884834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/678530-question-about-true-fae?p=882503#post882503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but a paranoid Freehold is going to be suspicious of anyone who cheats death too many times or shows up with one too many powerful tokens, no matter how good his excuse is this time<br /> <br /> There's always the chance they never suspect you at all though, which is why you roll</div> </div> </div> </div> They'd have to know you cheated death, so don't brag about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T13:1